export anchor LabReadoutStyle:
    number: 413
    screen: DatabaseConsole
    name: Lab readout
    idea: The console is an instrument bench of hairline framed readouts, so status shows as large thin measurements, tables as coded reagents, the query as numbered protocol steps, results as filled sample vials and history as a pass or fail run log.
    base: dark
    palette:
        bench: #0e1112, the page and the style sheet
        panel: #151a1c, readout cells and swatches
        hair: #343b3f, the 1px grid lines between cells and every rule
        tube: #22292c, empty vial glass and the scale track
        ink: #e9eef0, text
        muted: #a0aaaf, tags, codes, units and crop brackets
        acid: #d4f06a, readings, vial fill, the open table, keywords, Run assay and focus
        onAcid: #1c2600, text on acid
        pass: #8fe0b5, PASS
        fail: #ffa091, FAIL and its error, on #2a1a19
    type:
        Neutral grotesque, Helvetica Neue, Neue Haas Grotesk Text, Arial,
        Liberation Sans, base 14px at 1.5. Readings are 56px at 300 with
        tabular figures, vial values 40px at 300, the mode word 30px.
        Tags and codes use ui-monospace, IBM Plex Mono, at 11px caps with
        0.12em tracking, protocol steps 13.5px mono.
    layout:
        A header with Brightwork Data in bold and assay bench in light,
        and Specimen production-replica in mono on the right. The bench is
        a 12 column grid of cells divided by 1px hairlines, each cell with
        small corner crop brackets top left and bottom right and a mono tag
        row with a code on the left and a unit on the right. Row one has
        three readouts, R1 Mode with a padlock and Read-only replica, R2
        Replica lag as a big acid 2 s over a ten step scale with two lit,
        and R3 Connections as 14 active. Row two has Reagents, a ruled
        table coding the tables T1 to T5 with tasks T2 in acid and its
        columns as .1 to .6, beside Protocol, the SQL as seven numbered
        steps with dotted rules and Run assay and Duplicate buttons. Row
        three has Readings, three vials S-01 to S-03 filled to 2, 1 and 1
        with the value and project, and a summary of 3 rows, 38 ms and
        highest first, beside a Run log table of R-03 to R-01 with time,
        method and a tick PASS with duration or a cross FAIL on a red tinted
        row with the error. Below 1000px the wide cells go full width. On
        phones every cell stacks and the run code column hides.
    spacing: A 12 column grid with 1px gaps. 18px by 20px cell padding.
    density: Medium. Seven readout cells in four rows.
    corners: Square. Corner crop brackets mark each cell instead of rounding.
    borders: Only 1px hairlines in #343b3f, dotted between protocol steps.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        Drawn instruments. Vials with tick marks, a ten step scale, a
        padlock, a tick for PASS and a cross for FAIL beside the word.
    focus: A 1px acid outline offset 3px with a 4px soft acid halo.
    tone: Clinical lab words, such as Reagents, Protocol, Readings, Run assay and PASS.
